   246	
   247	<h2 id="stop">Stopping the link (runbook, written in E-2)</h2>
   248	<p>Two kinds of stop. <strong>A link/transport stop</strong> (the sender, the call, IAM): status logic is fine, so <code>recomputeStatuses</code> keeps running. <strong>A status/receiver-integrity stop</strong> (a bad <code>deriveStatus</code>, a bad projection, a bad receiver release): pause <code>recomputeStatuses</code> too, accepting that the <code>members</code> scheduler attestation stays red until recovery.</p>
   249	<ol>
   250	  <li><strong>Immediately</strong> (Christie, Console): pause <code>reconcileLink</code> (and, for an integrity stop, <code>recomputeStatuses</code>); on Cloud Run <code>ingestmemberupdate</code> → Permissions, remove <code>clayhub-link@</code>'s invoker (an emergency removal is allowed; granting by hand isn't, except Q9's recorded grant). Trigger deliveries then get 403, throw, and Eventarc retries them for up to 24 h; the sender-non-2xx alert fires (at most one email per hour).</li>
   251	  <li><strong>Then</strong> record it: a guarded release of <code>members</code> with <code>invoker: ["private"]</code> (sha phrase), attested (for a transport stop the schedule is still enabled, so the scheduler reading passes).</li>
   252	  <li><strong>To resume</strong>: fix the cause; guarded release(s); resume the paused job(s); Force run <code>reconcileLink</code> to catch up whatever the 24-hour retry window dropped; then attest.</li>
   253	  <li><strong>A stop email</strong> (409, recompute stop, or reconcile abort): read the logged counts and ids; check each id in Membership Manager. If the change is real (e.g. many pauses start on the 1st), create a <code>linkOverrides</code> doc for that one scope with limits just above the counts and an <code>expiresAt</code> within 24 h, then Force run the job; its use emails you. If it isn't real, stop the link and investigate. A reconcile <em>abort</em> (a live doc with no valid memberId) blocks catch-up and removals until that doc is fixed in Membership Manager.</li>
   254	</ol>
   255	
   256	<h2>Firebase safety checklist</h2>
   257	<ul>
   258	  <li>Every new collection gets an explicit rule and rules tests in the same commit as the code that writes it, deployed before the function (E-2, E-6).</li>
   259	  <li>Writers to my-clay-hub's member data: <code>ingestMemberUpdate</code> (single and reconcile) and <code>recomputeStatuses</code> (status and profile pause only) — both as <code>ingest@</code>, each change one transaction, never deletes.</li>
   260	  <li>Nothing writes to <code>tinker-hq-apps</code>: <code>clayhub-link@</code> holds only get/list; the codebase uses no write API (tested).</li>
   261	  <li>No forbidden field at any nesting level, and no full phone, crosses projects (contract + fixtures); no personal data in logs.</li>
   262	  <li>Emulator tests only; neither guard can reach the other project; the CLI credential file is never read.</li>
   263	  <li>Bulk changes bounded (Q8) and atomic: a reconcile and a recompute are each one transaction (≤ 250 members), so a stopped or failed run writes nothing.</li>
   264	</ul>
   265	
   266	<h2>Completeness check — if it's interrupted</h2>
   267	<ul>
   268	  <li>E-pre…E-4: docs and code on branches; nothing live until merged and deployed.</li>
   269	  <li>E-5 halfway: Console state is visible; re-read and continue. Nothing uses the accounts until E-6.</li>
   270	  <li>E-6 deployed, E-7 not: ingest is live with no caller — harmless.</li>
   271	  <li>E-7 released, E-8 not: <code>reconcileLink</code> is paused; triggers send each member whose doc is edited (once Q9's grant is in; before that they're refused and retried for 24 h); nothing reads the projection (no sign-in until Phase F).</li>
   272	  <li>K13 removed but delivery unproven: E-8 step 2 is the gate; if it fails, stop the link and re-plan — never restore broad grants.</li>
   273	</ul>
   274	
   275	<h2>Resume instructions</h2>
   276	<ul>
   277	  <li>Read Status and the newest Decisions-log entry.</li>
   278	  <li>Branches: <code>git -C ~/my-clay-hub branch -a</code>, <code>git -C ~/studio-hub branch -a</code> (names start <code>phase-e-</code>); open PRs and their review state.</li>
   279	  <li>Deploy state: each project's <code>scripts/deploy-functions.sh --status --codebase &lt;cb&gt;</code> (fetch first).</li>
   280	  <li>Reviews: <code>~/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/reviews/my-clay-hub-phase-e-plan-round&lt;n&gt;-*</code>.</li>
   281	</ul>
